From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: build without W=1 warnings

- Variables that were set but never read are removed; calls made only for
  such a variable stay as plain calls. Where only "#if 0" code reads one,
  it is marked __maybe_unused. rwnx_rxbuff_pattern was unused; the
  s_conn_state table in rwnx_defs.h is used by one of the files that
  include it.
- fdrv Makefile: -I$(srctree)/$(src) and its aic8800_bsp sibling point
  into the kernel tree, which has no such directories; removed.
- rwnx_plat_userconfig_parsing: a key name that does not fit is skipped
  instead of overflowing keyname with sprintf, and a value kstrtol cannot
  parse is no longer stored (val kept the previous key's value).

Machine code changes only in rwnx_plat_userconfig_parsing; everything else
differs only in line number and string offset constants.

